  "created": "2026-07-02T21:43:33.68Z",
  "description": "Post-quantum integration for ASP.NET Core Identity, with two surfaces at deliberately different scopes. (1) Argon2id password hashing for every deployment — PHC-formatted, secure-by-default work factors, transparent rehash-on-login, one-line PBKDF2→Argon2id migration via AddArgon2idPasswordHasherWithMigration, fail-closed verification with bounded parse cost, RFC 9106 §5.3 Known Answer Tests + reference-CLI PHC interop + emitter wire-format pin + deterministic generative fuzz corpus. Runs on net8.0 / net9.0 / net10.0. (2) Hybrid post-quantum JWT issuance for owned/trusted ecosystems (you control both the issuer and every verifier) — ML-DSA-65 signatures (FIPS 204) with optional X-Wing (X25519 + ML-KEM-768) encryption, kid-based key rotation, JSON-source-gen claim path, built on PostQuantum.Jwt 1.0.0 (stable). Uses non-IANA algorithm identifiers; intentionally not interoperable with generic JWT tooling until the IETF JOSE PQC drafts land. Requires .NET 10 (and OpenSSL 3.5+, 3.x series, on Linux). Supply chain: embedded CycloneDX SBOM, GitHub Sigstore-signed build-provenance attestation (verifiable with gh attestation verify), NuGet Trusted Publishing, deterministic SourceLink builds, .snupkg symbols, CodeQL, Dependabot. 1.0 is a semver API-stability commitment — NOT an audit claim; the library is not independently audited, stated plainly in SECURITY.md. See https://github.com/systemslibrarian/postquantum-identity for the full stance, migration guide, quantum-readiness playbook, and runnable issuer/verifier/key-tool samples.",
